# transformers is pinned to >=4.47,<4.50 in the Dockerfile because coqui-tts
# 0.26.0 imports APIs that later transformers releases removed
# (pytorch_utils.isin_mps_friendly, top-level BeamSearchScorer). The fixed
# releases below are all 5.x, which coqui-tts 0.26.0 cannot import.
#
# None of these is reachable here. The service only runs the Coqui VITS model
# tts_models/es/css10/vits, which is not a Hugging Face model: nothing loads a
# model or tokenizer through transformers, trust_remote_code is never used,
# and save_pretrained is never called. transformers is only imported at module
# scope by coqui-tts.
#
# Planned removal: upgrade to coqui-tts 0.28 (transformers >= 5.10) once the
# NVIDIA driver on the TTS host has been checked against the newer torch CUDA
# wheels. Delete these entries in that change.

# transformers: remote code execution (fixed in 5.3.0)
CVE-2026-4372
# transformers: trust_remote_code setting can be overridden (fixed in 5.5.0)
CVE-2026-5241
# transformers: save_pretrained path traversal via chat template names (fixed in 5.10.0)
CVE-2026-9856
